# Commit and push

After finishing work that adds or changes project files, commit and push to `origin` on the current branch without waiting to be asked.

- Use a short commit message that says why the change exists
- Never commit `.env`, `.env.local`, keys, or credentials
- Never skip git hooks
- Never force-push unless the user explicitly asks
- After the commit, `git push -u origin HEAD` if the branch has no upstream, otherwise `git push`
